Fix strand-dependent SVA fragment merging in ProcessRepeats (RepeatMasker 4.2.5).

Cycle 8 stops looking ahead for an SVA after three candidates that did not merge
(`last if ... $lookAhead++ > 2`), and only the SVA/LAVA branch gives the count back
(`$lookAhead--`). A candidate removed by the generic "Merging a joined pair" branch
keeps its count, so a forward-strand SVA whose VNTR fragments start just before the
VNTR range (consensus < 425) runs out of look-ahead and is reported as 2-4 lines
instead of one. Reverse-strand copies are unaffected, which makes RepeatMasker's
output depend on the element's orientation.

The "merge close fragments" branch removes a candidate the same way, so it gets the
same decrement. Not observed firing for SVAs; included so every branch that removes a
candidate in this loop gives its count back.

Not yet reported upstream. Applied only when building with --build-arg RM_SVA_PATCH=1.

--- a/ProcessRepeats
+++ b/ProcessRepeats
@@ -3183,6 +3183,7 @@
                 if ( $options{'source'} );
                 #print "REMOVING FROM PROXIMITY ITERATOR\n";
             $proxIter->remove();
+            $lookAhead--;  # a merged candidate must not use up the SVA look-ahead window
             if ( $DEBUG ) {
               print "  Outcome:\n";
               $currentAnnot->print();
@@ -3245,6 +3246,7 @@
             $currentAnnot->addDerivedFromAnnot( $next1Annot )
                 if ( $options{'source'} );
             $proxIter->remove();
+            $lookAhead--;  # same as the joined-pair merge above
             if ( $DEBUG ) {
               print "  Outcome:\n";
               $currentAnnot->print();
